  "visualReviewNotes": [
    "Actually inspected both whole-page contact sheets containing all 35 pages, all six readable caption-strip sheets containing pages 1-33, and all 17 selected full-page images. Consistent Bricolage typography, page numbering, source-link rows and margins remain readable without clipped or overlapping text.",
    "The cover explicitly names the 27 September community corrections. Downtown pages show the joined Voya podium and curved tower balconies, retaining uncertainty wording for dimensions and floor detail. The source-dated construction caption explicitly distinguishes future-envelope tree clearances from a dated construction survey.",
    "Lakeview full pages 14-17 visibly contain the terraced Harbourwalk form and additional purple low-rise rows, with consistent shadows and ground placement. Text names South Banks, Pier House and expanded Aura context while clearly retaining approximate heights and placement, unresolved municipal blocks, and the fact that not all five extra Aura rows tie to a current application. The waterfront and source terrain remain illustrative, and the layout does not claim complete village coverage.",
    "Port Credit pages 10 and 12 remain land-focused and their matched comparison cameras align. Uptown and Dixie pages retain coherent streets, transit colour conventions and building scale. The Absolute detail page retains its distinct twisting forms; no new visible loose or floating geometry appeared in these page renders.",
